Intercom read-only cross-context research

Workstream ID: ic-08
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Intercom/issues/7
Status: DONE (technical qualification; included in local .16, not human accepted)
Milestone: Spoken discovery to an illustrated local evidence report
Dependencies: ic-06

Purpose:
  Distinguish reading saved context/session evidence from contacting existing
  work sessions. Resolve spoken project names from mesh metadata, inspect
  available local evidence, explain relationships and open a private report.

Tasks:
  [x] Transcribe the owner's supplied recording locally before using its wording.
  [x] Add a strictly validated research intent without work actions.
  [x] Read registered continuity files and explicitly requested linked histories.
  [x] Generate a cited, illustrated, self-contained local HTML report.
  [x] Open only host-generated reports; surface opening and coverage failures.
  [x] Keep catalog diagnostics available without a wall of routing warnings.
  [x] Verify recorded wording, cancellation, access bounds and unchanged work safety.
  [x] Update affected documentation and owned continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
  The owner-recorded discovery request produces an evidence-backed local report
  without resuming or sending work to any existing session. Missing catalog
  names, unavailable workspaces and busy sessions do not prevent saved research.
  Notes, individual conversation evidence, indexed attribution and live
  conversational access remain distinct. Incomplete coverage is explicit.
  Audio and collected evidence stay local; only request text and minimal routing
  metadata enter the restricted controller. Existing tool permissions remain.
  The protected running .15 release is not restarted or overwritten.

Completion evidence:
  Superseding packaging milestone: integrated local .16 now includes this
  collection lane; ic09 adds observed activity and optional cited synthesis.
  Current57host/53desktop,8packaged cases and actual portable smoke pass.
  Earlier source-only/no-package receipts below describe original qualification.
  The supplied recording is 82.9 seconds. Bundled local recognition returned provisional
  English text through two <=45-second segments with two seconds of overlap.
  This is offline recorded-input preparation, not extended live capture support.
  Detailed recording/transcript receipts remain private.
  Real restricted-controller interpretation and saved-evidence collection pass
  without constructing a work transport or requesting tool permission.
  41 contexts inspected; 173 files read, nine readable histories, four matching
  histories and eight contexts with references. Partial coverage is explicit,
  including 25 unavailable/partial source checks. This is not universal history
  coverage or proof that all reference contexts did project work.
  Desktop/mobile report checks and OS handler acceptance pass. Original input
  and retained .15 EXE hashes remain unchanged. Actual visible owner browser
  state was not automated. Detailed reports/receipts remain private.
  Final lint/build,16renderer/11controller/49host/47desktop cases pass.
  No new package, publication, tracking write or human acceptance is claimed.

Completion log:
  2026-11-12: Implemented and technically verified the bounded research lane.
  Fixed Windows file identity checks, streamed large histories with explicit
  parser gaps, improved extractive paragraphs and prioritized direct matches.
  Bounded feedback keeps essential Talk controls reachable. The initial UI
  overflow and subsequent lint failure were corrected before final checks.
  Source-only; running .15 and published .12 stay unchanged. Human report/
  speech acceptance, broader history discovery and semantic synthesis are not
  claimed. Remote issue/Project synchronization remains separately pending.
